NAME
       mytool - one line saying what mytool does

SYNOPSIS
       mytool [-v] [-o file] [input ...]
       mytool -h | --help

DESCRIPTION
       mytool reads each input, or the standard input when none is named, and writes the result to the standard output.

       A second paragraph explains the model the reader needs: what goes in, what comes out, and what is never changed.

OPTIONS
       -v     Report each input on the standard error as it is read.

       -o file
              Write to file instead of the standard output.

       -h     Print a short usage summary.

       --help Show this manual.

EXAMPLES
       Process two files into one:

       mytool -o all.txt one.txt two.txt

ENVIRONMENT
       MYTOOL_OPTS
              Options read before those on the command line.

EXIT STATUS
        CODE   MEANING
       ------+-------------------------------------------------------------
           0   success
           1   an input could not be read; the others were still processed
           2   a usage error

SEE ALSO
       roffsub(7)
